{
  "profile": {
    "name": "Ugakid RANO",
    "shortName": "RANO",
    "tagline": "Street grit. Raw emotion. The pulse of African-city life.",
    "location": "Kampala, Uganda",
    "genre": "Afro-Pop \u00b7 Hip-Hop \u00b7 Rap",
    "bio": [
      "RANO is a Ugandan rapper, singer and storyteller whose music blends street grit, raw emotion and the pulse of everyday African-city life. Switching effortlessly between English, Luganda, Runyakitara, Kiswahili and urban slang, his style captures both the hustle of the city and the soul of East Africa.",
      "He first caught attention with 'Rolex Guy', a playful anthem inspired by Uganda's beloved street food as a symbol of love, hustle and identity. With 'Somebody Come', he breaks the silence on mental health and the struggles of youth searching for light in dark places.",
      "Beyond music, RANO is a fearless performer who weaves comedy, social commentary and authentic UG flavour into his art. His debut Rolexperience event reflected his vision of turning culture into a movement \u2014 uniting people through street food, music and shared stories.",
      "With every verse, Ugakid carries the spirit of the underdog \u2014 bold, unfiltered and unapologetically real."
    ],
